    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000369 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000369">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002616"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid1215"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The corpus striatum (striated body) is a compound structure consisting of the caudate nucleus and the lentiform nucleus, which consists of the putamen and the globus pallidus[WP].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Thus, certain telencephalic characters - such as the presence of a pallium divided into lateral, dorsal, and medial formations and a subpallium divided into striatum and septum - appear to characterize all vertebrates. They are primitive characters and are homologous among all vertebrates.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000013>The term has been used in a few different ways: * It is a pair of nuclear masses which form the basal ganglia, along with the subthalamic nucleus and the substantia nigra. * It may also refer to both the basal ganglia and internal capsule collectively.[2]</obo:UBPROP_0000013>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>UBERON:0010082</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:CSTR</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0001311</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CALOHA:TS-0183</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EFO:0000381</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0000596</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
