        <owl:annotatedTarget>Organ with organ cavity which consists of the vestibular labyrinth and the cochlear labyrinth. The membranous labyrinth is lodged within the bony labyrinth and has the same general form; it is, however, considerably smaller and is partly separated from the bony walls by a quantity of fluid, the perilymph.[FMA, WP].</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:61022</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Membranous_labyrinth</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
