        <obo:IAO_0000115>The hippocampal sulcus, also known as the hippocampal fissure, is a sulcus that separates the dentate gyrus from the subiculum and the CA1 field in the hippocampus. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000012>two classes in ncit (in general ncit distinguishes between fissure and sulcus, whereas FMA treats these as exact synonyms)</obo:UBPROP_0000012>
