    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002911 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002911">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002616"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010262"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The parietal operculum, forming the superior bank of the sylvian fissure, as studied in the cat, contains the secondary somatosensory representation, &apos;S-II&apos;, and a second somatotopic representation (parietal ventral, or PV). Anatomically, primate S-II receives inputs from area 3 and area 1, and projects to PV and area 7. PV has projections to area 5 and premotor areas. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>PAO</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:PaOp</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:pao</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BIRNLEX:4029</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:13230</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
