        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0011233</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Alternate def: A synovial sheath is a layer of a tendon sheath containing tendons in the hand and foot. They lie internal to the fibrous tendon sheaths. An example is the common synovial sheath for the flexor tendons. [Wikipedia:Synovial_sheath]</rdfs:comment>
