        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fissure that divides the culmen lobule (lobules IV and V).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:RO_0002174 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>The culmen lobule (lobules IV/V) is a single structure in humans, but it is divided by the intraculminate fissure in many rodents. In some mouse strains such as SLJ/J, the intraculminate fissure is absent, in some strains such as DBA/2J it is present, and other strains (C57BL/10J and BALB/cJ) exhibit considerable variablility (PMID: 1953602).[MP]</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:266441729</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:83737</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HBA:9409</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>RadLex:RID6872</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:369052000</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>neuronames:1995</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>fissura intraculminalis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>intraculminate fissure</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ICF</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0035922</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>intraculminate fissure of cerebellum</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>intraculminate fissure of cerebellum</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
